      <div class="post-meta">New Launch · 25 July 2026 · 6 min read · ProjectHome.sg Editorial Team</div>
      <h1>Is This Novena&rsquo;s Most Capital-Resilient New Launch? An Honest Deep Dive Into The Serra Residences.</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="post-content">
    <img src="/assets/images/serra-residences-cover.jpg" alt="The Serra Residences — Transurban Properties' 133-unit, 28-storey freehold boutique launch at 7 Bassein Road in District 11, Novena, Singapore" loading="eager" decoding="async" />

    <p style="font-style:italic; color:var(--muted);">A ~6 minute read for buyers weighing up the first freehold, GFA-harmonised new launch in Novena &mdash; before the showflat marketing takes over.</p>

    <div style="background:var(--paper); border-left:4px solid var(--copper); padding:24px 28px; border-radius:0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0; margin:1.5em 0 2em;">
      <strong style="color:var(--teal); display:block; margin-bottom:8px;">TL;DR</strong>
      <p style="margin-bottom:0;"><strong>The Serra Residences</strong> is Transurban Properties&rsquo; freehold boutique launch at <strong>7 Bassein Road, District 11</strong> &mdash; a single 28-storey tower of <strong>133 units</strong> designed by P&amp;T Consultants (Park Nova, Grand Dunman) with 932 Design interiors and ECOPLAN landscape. It&rsquo;s the <strong>first freehold, GFA-harmonised new launch in the Core Central Region</strong>, a 9-minute walk (742&nbsp;m) to <strong>Novena MRT</strong>, and inside the 1&nbsp;km catchment for both <strong>St. Joseph&rsquo;s Institution Junior (0.59&nbsp;km)</strong> and <strong>Hong Wen School (1.0&nbsp;km)</strong>. On the NAVIS PrimeKey Analysis it scores <strong>34 / 40 (85%) &mdash; 4.2 out of 5 stars</strong>: five-star marks on GLS pipeline, tenure, yield, school effect and MOP upgrader cluster. The lone drag: a 2-star project-size score reflecting boutique liquidity (133 units). Verdict: <strong>Strong Buy for legacy-holders, yield-focused CCR investors and education-led families</strong>. Preview window opens <strong>19 September 2026</strong> &middot; Sale launch day <strong>3 October 2026</strong>.</p>
    </div>

    <p>Novena has always held a special status among Singapore&rsquo;s residential enclaves &mdash; a distinct balance of high-end medical convenience, prestigious schools and quiet leafy streets, where properties tend to be tightly held. And if you&rsquo;ve been looking for a brand-new freehold opportunity here, you already know how scarce the options are. Along Bassein Road specifically, the last completed private residential development landed more than a decade ago in 2015.</p>

    <p>Enter <strong>The Serra Residences</strong>, an exclusive boutique launch by Transurban Properties with a preview opening <strong>19 September 2026</strong> and sale launch day on <strong>3 October 2026</strong>. A single 28-storey tower at 7 Bassein Road, meticulously curated into just 133 units.</p>

    <p>But does it deserve a spot in your wealth-preservation portfolio, or is it just another boutique launch dressed up in a good address? Below we walk through the three real-estate moats that separate this project from the field, then run it through the <a href="/blog/primekey-analysis-introduction">NAVIS PrimeKey Analysis</a> &mdash; our 8-pillar framework for grading any Singapore project on data, not on hype.</p>

    <h2>Quick project facts</h2>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Developer:</strong> Transurban Properties Pte Ltd</li>
      <li><strong>Tenure:</strong> Freehold</li>
      <li><strong>Site area:</strong> 4,774.80&nbsp;sqm / 51,396&nbsp;sqft &middot; Gross plot ratio 2.8</li>
      <li><strong>Total units:</strong> 133 (boutique-scale, single 28-storey tower over 1 basement)</li>
      <li><strong>Carpark:</strong> 106 lots (including 5 EV lots)</li>
      <li><strong>District:</strong> D11 &mdash; Novena / Newton (Core Central Region)</li>
      <li><strong>Nearest MRT:</strong> Novena MRT (NS20, North-South Line) &mdash; <strong>9-min walk, ~742&nbsp;m</strong> to Exit A</li>
      <li><strong>Schools within 1&nbsp;km:</strong> St. Joseph&rsquo;s Institution Junior (0.59&nbsp;km) &middot; Hong Wen School (1.0&nbsp;km) &middot; 9 primary and secondary schools within 2&nbsp;km</li>
      <li><strong>Design team:</strong> P&amp;T Consultants (Park Nova, Grand Dunman) &middot; 932 Design interiors (One Holland Village Residences) &middot; ECOPLAN Asia landscape (Leedon Green, Alex Residences)</li>
      <li><strong>Unit mix:</strong> Lower register (L4&ndash;L16) &mdash; 2-Bedroom + Study (710&ndash;721&nbsp;sqft), 3-Bedroom (764&ndash;904&nbsp;sqft), 4-Bedroom (958&nbsp;sqft) &middot; Upper register (L18&ndash;L28) &mdash; 4-Bedroom / 4BR+Study (1,216&ndash;1,335&nbsp;sqft), 4BR Premium with private lift (1,529&nbsp;sqft), 5BR Premium with private lift (1,755&nbsp;sqft), Penthouses (2,670&ndash;2,820&nbsp;sqft) &middot; L17 Sky Terrace</li>
      <li><strong>Preview window:</strong> opens 19 September 2026</li>
      <li><strong>Sale launch day:</strong> 3 October 2026</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The 3 core investment pillars</h2>

    <p>Before the scoring system, the three real-estate moats that make this District 11 launch unusual.</p>

    <h3>1. The GFA-harmonisation quantum leap &mdash; no paid space wastage</h3>

    <p>For years, Singapore property buyers reluctantly paid hundreds of thousands of dollars for non-livable spaces &mdash; oversized aircon ledges, deep planters, double-volume voids counted into your PSF. The Serra Residences rewrites the playbook as the <strong>first freehold, GFA-harmonised new launch in the Core Central Region</strong>.</p>

    <p>Under the latest GFA-harmonisation guidelines, developers can only charge for actual livable, usable floor space. At The Serra Residences, every square foot you&rsquo;re paying for is maximised for day-to-day liveability and value. That&rsquo;s a structural pricing-efficiency advantage over older freehold projects where &ldquo;phantom space&rdquo; made up a meaningful slice of the purchase price.</p>

    <h3>2. Positioned in a hyper-vibrant healthcare &amp; lifestyle corridor</h3>

    <p>Bassein Road is a uniquely quiet sanctuary that sits minutes away from two of the country&rsquo;s most significant masterplans. Residents get an easy 8&ndash;9-minute stroll (about 742&nbsp;m) to <strong>Novena MRT Station (Exit A)</strong>, one stop from Newton interchange and four stops from Orchard.</p>

    <p>More importantly, the site sits right beside <strong>Health City Novena</strong> &mdash; Singapore&rsquo;s first mega-integrated healthcare masterplan &mdash; which will bring thousands of high-earning medical professionals into the immediate catchment. That&rsquo;s a robust, built-in tenant pool that few CCR sites can match. Layer on the upcoming lifestyle enclave <strong>&ldquo;The New Dempsey&rdquo; at 2 Moulmein Road</strong> just a 3-minute walk away, and you have an unusual combination of absolute medical utility <em>and</em> premium lifestyle retail on the same doorstep &mdash; the kind of overlap that supports both capital growth and rentability through cycles.</p>

    <h3>3. The elite 1&nbsp;km double-school advantage</h3>

    <p>Proximity to elite primary schools is one of the most ironclad price stabilisers in Singapore property. Values near popular schools are notoriously resilient during market downturns. The Serra Residences strikes gold here, sitting comfortably within the coveted 1&nbsp;km radius of <strong>St. Joseph&rsquo;s Institution (SJI) Junior at just 0.59&nbsp;km</strong> and <strong>Hong Wen School at 1.0&nbsp;km</strong>. With <strong>9 primary and secondary schools within 2&nbsp;km</strong> plus tertiary anchors like the <strong>Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (NTU)</strong> nearby, families are looking at a multi-decade educational runway.</p>

