    <p>Strip away the launch noise and the buyer profile resolves cleanly:</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Legacy-holders &amp; multigenerational families.</strong> A freehold in prime D11 with a Sky Terrace, tennis court and full facility slate at 28 storeys is the kind of asset that gets held, not flipped. If the plan is to pass the property to the next generation, tenure trumps everything else &mdash; and The Serra delivers on that.</li>
      <li><strong>Yield-focused CCR investors.</strong> A 3.5% projected gross yield in a freehold, Novena-adjacent, MRT-walk, school-catchment asset is a rare combination. The Health City Novena + Mount Elizabeth Novena + Tan Tock Seng + NTU School of Medicine cluster produces a permanent, high-budget tenant pool.</li>
      <li><strong>Education-led affluent families.</strong> The SJI Junior 0.59&nbsp;km catchment plus 9 schools within 2&nbsp;km is one of the most defensible school-catchment overlaps in the CCR. If P1 admission drives your property decision, this is a shortcut to the front of the queue.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>It&rsquo;s a weaker fit if you want mega-resort facilities with hundreds of pool decks, or if your underwriting relies on fast resale flips with hyper-liquid transaction volumes. This is deliberately a boutique asset for a discerning buyer who values exclusivity, structural pricing efficiency, and prime freehold real estate.</p>

    <p>As always, the responsible next step is to <em>see the data before you see the showflat</em>. Open the PrimeKey Report above, line it up against any other CCR shortlist you&rsquo;re considering, and decide on facts &mdash; not on the brochure&rsquo;s rendering quality.</p>

